"cues": [
{
"block": "b1",
"t": 3.2,
"end": 10.851,
"text": "Emma saves a purchase order, and Ledgerline stops her: ERR-PO-0412."
},
{
"block": "b1",
"t": 11.466,
"end": 13.742,
"text": "What does it mean, and how does she fix it?"
},
{
"block": "b1",
"t": 14.276,
"end": 17.178,
"text": "The answer is in Northbridge's documents."
},
{
"block": "b2",
"t": 17.778,
"end": 25.962,
"text": "Here they are: 693 files of PDFs, spreadsheets, e-mails, service definitions and scans."
},
{
"block": "b2",
"t": 26.462,
"end": 32.081,
"text": "4.69 million tokens: far too much to send with every question."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 32.681,
"end": 41.446,
"text": "First, we parse, with a reader for each kind of file: PDFs keep their pages and headings, and spreadsheet rows keep their column names."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 41.946,
"end": 46.102,
"text": "All 464 facts we check survive."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 46.702,
"end": 54.085,
"text": "Then we chunk, along each document's own structure: about 200 tokens a piece, with 15 percent overlap."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 54.585,
"end": 59.844,
"text": "The quick-reference card for this error, QRC-03, becomes three chunks."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 60.344,
"end": 63.049,
"text": "The whole pile: 28,953."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 63.649,
"end": 65.274,
"text": "Next, two indexes."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 65.774,
"end": 72.344,
"text": "An embedding model turns each chunk into 384 numbers, a point in space, kept in Chroma."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 72.844,
"end": 77.999,
"text": "And BM25 remembers which chunks contain which exact words."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 78.599,
"end": 79.69,
"text": "Now Emma's question."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 80.294,
"end": 90.476,
"text": "In vector space, its nearest neighbours are purchase-order services and ERR-MAT-0412: close in meaning, but the wrong code."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 91.01,
"end": 97.361,
"text": "BM25 matches the exact words, and puts QRC-03 first."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 97.961,
"end": 104.961,
"text": "Then a reranker reads the question beside each of the top 20, and puts them in order: 57 milliseconds."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 105.461,
"end": 115.701,
"text": "A right source in the top five: vectors alone, 56 percent; keywords, 77; keywords and the reranker, 89."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 116.301,
"end": 128.456,
"text": "The top ten go into the prompt, numbered, and the model answers from them, with citations: a supplier outside the UK needs VAT20-RC, then press F8 again."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 128.956,
"end": 133.345,
"text": "Search, 45 milliseconds. Answer, 12 seconds."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 133.945,
"end": 139.854,
"text": "That is RAG: parse, chunk, index, search, rerank, answer."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 140.389,
"end": 145.311,
"text": "87 percent of the golden set answered correctly, a quarter of a cent each."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 145.926,
"end": 150.291,
"text": "Its hard case is Emma's Brightcell question, spread over eleven sources."
},
{
"block": "b9",
"t": 150.791,
"end": 152.289,
"text": "The search finds two."
}
]
}